// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 3 „Päev, kell ja harjumused” (a2-011…015), stage A2 algus (lessons 001–020).
// Methodology v5 for A2 (docs/METHODOLOGY_A2_V5.md, normative; strictModulesV5.json „a2”), made on the model of modules
// 1–2: one real communicative outcome a lesson, one input, ≤ 5 / 4 / 5 blocks a sheet and ≤ 14 a lesson in a 60-minute
// lesson; the module control is one sheet (≤ 10 blocks, 45 min). Lengths of the stage: input text 80–120 words, audio
// ≤ 75 s, writing 20–45 words, speech 35–60 s (a pair card up to 120 s). At most one short dictation a lesson (≤ 6
// sentences), here in 012 (the time); 011, 013 and 014 have a true/false meaning task instead. Ready phrases (tipText, role-card phrases, a given opening) help in 011–013 and are gone from the
// main speaking and writing of 014, the module's last teaching lesson. One learning picture per teaching lesson carries
// its pair task (art/visuals/a2-module-03.js). No lesson uses the continuing story's cast (G7).
//   011 LUGU R→S  „Minu päev” — a baker's text about his day (reading). Outcome: tell about your ordinary day and ask
//                 about another person's (ma lähen / ta läheb / nad lähevad; hommikul, õhtul, öösel); the four
//                 neighbours' cards are the guessing game; an interview and a short story for the school's paper.
//   012 RÄÄK L→S  „Mis kell?” — a phone call to a hairdresser (listening). Outcome: say and ask the time (pool kolm,
//                 veerand neli, kolmveerand viis), read opening hours (kella kümnest kuueni) and book a time on the
//                 phone; the dental clinic's administrator holds hidden information (G9).
//   013 KIRJ R→W  „Kui tihti?” — a flat-share ad „Otsin korterikaaslast!” (reading). Outcome: say how often you do
//                 things (alati … mitte kunagi, kaks korda nädalas, käin ujumas; the verb second after a time word) and
//                 answer the ad in writing; the three candidates' week charts are the pair decision.
//   014 PROJ L→W  „Minu nädal” — a friend's voice message (listening). Outcome: agree a meeting time without notes or
//                 phrases (esmaspäeval, esmaspäeviti, nädalavahetusel; kõigepealt, siis, pärast seda) and write to your
//                 own teacher when you can come next week (a real addressee, G13); two week planners = information gap.
//   015 EKS       Control 3 (one sheet, 45 min): reading, listening, writing and speaking, 10 points each; raw points, the
//                 Harno scale (× 2), the thresholds named one way, the result of control 2 beside it.
// Removed blocks stay in this file as hide(block, why) — ids and learners' answers are kept, and the practice engine
// (practice/engine/extract.js) still builds Harjuta items from their form tasks. The previous version (template v4, one
// storyline through the whole module) is in git history (main before this PR).
import { B, hide, tag, teach, why, withShapes } from '../blocks.js';

export const MODULE = { id: 'a2-module-03', course: 'a2', title: 'Päev, kell ja harjumused', level: 'A2', design: 'v2', template: 'v4' };

// one line for every block taken off the sheets by the v5 rewrite
const V5_CUT = 'v5 (2026-11-25): lehelt maha — tunni eelarve (60 min), üks sisend, loo tegelased ainult ühes tunnis';
const V5_DRILL = 'v5 (2026-11-25): drill Harjutasse — lehelt maha, ülesanded jäävad Harjuta harjutusteks';
// a recording is heard twice (methodV5.js G6); in the control the player is locked
const twice = (block, lock = false) => ({ ...block, data: { ...block.data, plays: 2, ...(lock ? { lockPlays: true } : {}) } });
// a block beside another one on the page (two columns)
const half = (block) => ({ ...block, width: 'half', span: 6 });
// a check is one sheet with its own label (no „Avasta” subtitle)
const checkSheet = (label, subtitle) => ({ discover: { label, slot: 1, subtitle } });
// a real addressee (methodV5.js G13): the learner sends the text to a real person
const toAddressee = (block, who) => ({ ...block, data: { ...block.data, realAddressee: who } });
// the thresholds, named one way everywhere (METHODOLOGY_A2_V5.md §2.9)
const THRESHOLDS = 'Harno: eksam on sooritatud alates 60 %-st ja ükski osa ei tohi olla 0 punkti. KeeleSepp: eksamiks valmis alates 70 %-st, meie sertifikaat alates 80 %-st (sisemine lävi, et eksamil oleks varu).';

